[[2047,127,8192,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The optional services relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls\nthe heating circuit for the seats as well as the electric rear windows\nand sun roof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234128\">E3060</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The coil for relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 is energized when\nthe ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse F6 of supplementary\nfuse box B98 B, whilst the supply at the relay contact arrives from\nthe battery, through the line for maxifuse J/B2 of B99.</strong></p><p>This supply passes through fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              of\nsupplementary fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 C</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which guarantees the protection\nof the circuit and reaches the switch on the seat via the connections \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D70B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D71B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : the supply for the device is therefore controlled\nby the ignition (INT/A); and is also connected to earth.</p><p>When the switch on the seat is pressed,\ncommand signals (positive and negative) are sent to the motors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N32</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              (driver&#x27;s\nside) and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N33</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              (passenger side): reversing the signals according\nto the contact which is closed determines the direction of the rotation\nof the actual motor.</p>"]]